{# Not a macro — a whole manifest. `k8s/manifests` renders this file as `service.yaml` for
   every role that names `service.yaml` in its `manifests_files` and ships no
   `templates/service.yaml.j2` of its own (`manifests_shared_defaults` in that role's
   defaults). This file is the three-line wrapper around the `service()` macro below that
   22 roles' Service templates would otherwise repeat byte for byte.

   THE ENTRY IS THE INPUT. Name and port come from the role's `containers_list` entry, and the
   two variants those 22 roles differed on are entry keys rather than template edits:

     service_port_name    the Service's port NAME (home-assistant, homelab-mcp, zigbee2mqtt).
                          Omit for the plain unnamed form every other role renders.
     service_extra_ports  [{name, port}] for a sidecar's port — the exportarr metrics port on
                          sonarr, radarr and prowlarr. Kubernetes REJECTS a Service mixing
                          named and unnamed ports and rejects it at APPLY time, after every
                          repo-side check has read green, so the macro names the primary port
                          itself whenever this is non-empty.

   A role whose Service does not fit keeps its own `templates/service.yaml.j2`, which wins
   over this file. `ansible/templates/service.yml.j2`'s header lists the five disqualifiers
   and names the role behind each. #}
{% from 'service.yml.j2' import service with context %}
---
{{ service(
     container_item.name,
     container_item.port,
     port_name=container_item.service_port_name | default(none),
     extra_ports=container_item.service_extra_ports | default([])
   ) -}}
